---
// 2026-09-06: the public site is now **this page**. The owner: *"in webapp I
// want to do major design changes. i want single paged website here. it will
// have about section, services, recent three blogs, recent three workshops,
// and top three testimonials."*
//
// What was here before was a stub — a heading, one sentence, and a contact
// form whose backend had already been deleted (D-32) — while About and
// Services each held one paragraph on a route of their own. Those two pages
// are gone; their copy lives in the sections below, at `#about` and
// `#services`.
//
// ## The three content strips are the listing pages' own islands
//
// `LiveBlogList`, `LiveWorkshopList` and `LiveTestimonialList` are reused
// exactly as `/blog`, `/workshops` and `/testimonials` use them — seeded
// server-side from a build-time fetch, reconciled client-side so something
// published since the last deploy still appears. The only difference is a
// `limit` of three and a heading level of 3 (see each prop's own comment).
// Nothing here re-fetches or re-formats content on its own; a second way to
// render a blog post is exactly the drift that would make the homepage and
// the archive disagree.
//
// ## "Older blogs and workshops" links are same-origin
//
// The owner named `https://nourishthenerve.com/en/blog` and `.../en/workshops`.
// Those are *this site's* pages — `site-config.ts`'s `siteUrl` is that apex —
// so they are written as `/{locale}/blog` and `/{locale}/workshops`. An
// absolute apex URL would jump a visitor from `next.`, from staging, or from
// an ephemeral PR environment straight into production.
import { supportedLocales, t } from '@ndn/i18n';
import type { Locale } from '@ndn/i18n';
import { Card, Heading, Link, VisuallyHidden } from '@ndn/ui';

import { fetchPublishedBlogPosts } from '../../blog/content-client.js';
import { LiveBlogList } from '../../blog/LiveBlogList.js';
import { services } from '../../config/services.js';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  siteName,
  whatsappBusinessNumber,
  whatsappChatUrl,
} from '../../site-config.js';
import { LiveTestimonialList } from '../../testimonials/LiveTestimonialList.js';
import { fetchPublishedTestimonials } from '../../testimonials/testimonial-client.js';
import { LiveWorkshopList } from '../../workshops/LiveWorkshopList.js';
import { fetchPublishedWorkshops } from '../../workshops/workshop-client.js';

/**
 * How many blog posts and workshops the landing page shows before handing
 * off to the archive.
 *
 * **Testimonials no longer use it** (2026-09-07): the principal picks those
 * by hand, so their count is a decision made in `account/testimonials`, not
 * a constant here. See the strip's own comment.
 */
const HOME_LIST_LIMIT = 3;

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  // Three independent build-time fetches, in parallel. None of the three
  // clients throws — each returns an empty list when the content API is
  // unreachable (the ephemeral PR environment has no NdnDataStack at all),
  // so a build never depends on content existing.
  const [posts, workshops, testimonials] = await Promise.all([
    fetchPublishedBlogPosts(),
    fetchPublishedWorkshops(),
    fetchPublishedTestimonials(),
  ]);
  return supportedLocales.map((locale) => ({
    params: { locale },
    props: { posts, workshops, testimonials },
  }));
}

const { locale } = Astro.params as { locale: Locale };
const { posts, workshops, testimonials } = Astro.props as {
  posts: Awaited<ReturnType<typeof fetchPublishedBlogPosts>>;
  workshops: Awaited<ReturnType<typeof fetchPublishedWorkshops>>;
  testimonials: Awaited<ReturnType<typeof fetchPublishedTestimonials>>;
};

// A post or workshop not yet translated into this locale doesn't appear —
// the same filter `/blog` and `/workshops` apply to their own seeds. Moot
// while `supportedLocales` is `['en']`, correct once it isn't.
const postsForLocale = posts.filter((post) => post.translations[locale] !== undefined);
const workshopsForLocale = workshops.filter(
  (workshop) => workshop.details[locale] !== undefined,
);

// `set:html`, not a literal `<style>...</style>` block — the convention
// Nav.astro and Footer.astro already document.
//
// ## 2026-09-07: the theme, on the page it was designed for
//
// Every colour below is one of `packages/ui`'s tokens; there is no hex here
// any more. The bands alternate paper / olive / paper / olive with the
// testimonials on lavender, which is the one place the accent hue gets a
// whole section rather than a detail — quotes are the warmest thing on the
// page and the lavender is the warmest ground.
//
// Three things here are load-bearing rather than decorative:
//
//   * `.ndn-home-grid > astro-island { display: contents }`. Astro wraps a
//     `client:*` island in an `<astro-island>` element, so the cards a list
//     renders are that element's children, not the grid's — without this the
//     whole strip collapses into one grid cell. Astro does emit the same
//     declaration itself, but only as an **inline** `<style>` inside the
//     island, and this repo's CSP is the reason `csp-inline-scripts.test.ts`
//     exists: inline content here lives or dies by an allow-list. Restating
//     it in the page's own stylesheet means the layout does not depend on
//     that. Scoped to this grid rather than set on `astro-island` globally,
//     which would also change how the site nav's own island lays out.
//   * The call-to-action selectors are `.ndn-home a.ndn-home-cta`, not
//     `.ndn-home-cta`. `packages/ui`'s `.ndn-link` (underlined, brand
//     coloured) has the same specificity as a bare class would, and which of
//     the two wins would then depend on stylesheet order.
//   * The heading sizes are written `.ndn-home .ndn-home-hero h1` rather than
//     `.ndn-home-hero h1`. `primitiveStylesCss` now sets a real type scale on
//     `h1.ndn-heading`/`h2.ndn-heading` (0,1,1), which the old two-part
//     selectors merely tied with — leaving which one won down to the order
//     Astro happens to emit two `<style>` elements in. (0,2,1) settles it.
const homeStylesCss = `
.ndn-home {
  --ndn-home-measure: 68rem;
}

.ndn-home-inner {
  max-width: var(--ndn-home-measure);
  margin-inline: auto;
}

/* The hero is the only place the mark appears at size. On a wide viewport it
   sits beside the copy; below that the column collapses and the mark is
   hidden outright rather than stacked — a 200px illustration between a
   headline and its call to action is a scroll a phone visitor has to make
   before reaching the thing the page is for. */
.ndn-home-hero {
  padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 10vw, 6.5rem);
  padding-inline: 1.25rem;
  background-image: linear-gradient(
    155deg,
    var(--ndn-color-surface-accent) 0%,
    var(--ndn-color-surface) 45%,
    var(--ndn-color-brand-wash) 100%
  );
  border-block-end: 1px solid var(--ndn-color-border);
}

.ndn-home-hero .ndn-home-inner {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 2rem;
  align-items: center;
}

.ndn-home-hero-mark {
  display: none;
}

@media (min-width: 56rem) {
  .ndn-home-hero .ndn-home-inner {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .ndn-home-hero-mark {
    display: block;
    justify-self: center;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 17rem;
    height: auto;
  }
}

.ndn-home .ndn-home-hero h1 {
  font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5.5vw, 3.5rem);
  line-height: 1.08;
  max-width: 20ch;
  margin-block: 0 1.25rem;
}

.ndn-home-lede {
  font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 2vw, 1.1875rem);
  line-height: 1.65;
  color: var(--ndn-color-text-muted);
  max-width: 54ch;
  margin-block: 0 2rem;
}

.ndn-home-section {
  padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  padding-inline: 1.25rem;
}

.ndn-home-section--tinted {
  background-color: var(--ndn-color-surface-muted);
}

/* The testimonials band, and the only full section on the lavender. */
.ndn-home-section--accent {
  background-color: var(--ndn-color-surface-accent);
}

.ndn-home .ndn-home-section h2 {
  font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
  margin-block: 0 0.75rem;
}

/* A short rule above each section heading, in the section's own accent. It
   is a ::before on the heading rather than a border on the section so it
   starts at the text rather than at the band edge, and it is decorative in
   the strict sense: no content, nothing announced. */
.ndn-home-section h2::before {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  width: 2.5rem;
  height: 2px;
  margin-block-end: 1.25rem;
  background-color: var(--ndn-color-brand);
}

.ndn-home-section--accent h2::before {
  background-color: var(--ndn-color-accent);
}

.ndn-home .ndn-home-section h3 {
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  margin-block: 0 0.375rem;
}

.ndn-home-intro,
.ndn-home-prose p {
  color: var(--ndn-color-text-muted);
  line-height: 1.75;
  max-width: 62ch;
  margin-block: 0 1rem;
}

/* auto-fill, not auto-fit: with one published workshop, auto-fit collapses
   the empty tracks and stretches that single card across the whole row,
   which reads as a banner rather than as one of three. auto-fill keeps the
   tracks, so a strip of one, two or three cards is the same card width. */
.ndn-home-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
  gap: 1.25rem;
  margin-block: 2rem 1.75rem;
}

.ndn-home-grid > astro-island {
  display: contents;
}

.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  transition: border-color var(--ndn-motion-duration-base) ease,
    box-shadow var(--ndn-motion-duration-base) ease,
    transform var(--ndn-motion-duration-base) ease;
}

/* Lifts by two pixels, not four, and the shadow is the border token blurred
   rather than a black wash — on a warm ground a grey shadow reads as dirt.
   Every duration in the transition above is a motion token, so under
   prefers-reduced-motion the card arrives at this state without travelling
   to it (tokens/motion.ts collapses all three at once). */
.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card:hover {
  border-color: var(--ndn-color-brand);
  box-shadow: 0 6px 20px var(--ndn-color-border);
  transform: translateY(-2px);
}

.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card p {
  color: var(--ndn-color-text-muted);
  line-height: 1.65;
  margin-block: 0;
}

.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  border-radius: 0.5rem;
}

/* A quote is the one piece of copy on this page set in the display serif at
   body size — it is someone speaking, not the site explaining. */
.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card blockquote {
  margin: 0;
  border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--ndn-color-accent);
  padding-inline-start: 1.125rem;
}

.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card blockquote p {
  color: var(--ndn-color-text);
  font-family: var(--ndn-font-family-display);
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  line-height: 1.45;
}

.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card blockquote footer {
  margin-block-start: 0.875rem;
  font-size: 0.8125rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ndn-color-text-muted);
}

/* Pushes a card own link to the bottom edge so a row of cards with
   different amounts of text still lines its links up. align-self keeps the
   anchor hit area to its text rather than the full card width, which a
   column flex container would otherwise stretch it to. (No backticks in
   this block: it is a JS template literal.) */
.ndn-home-grid .ndn-card > .ndn-link:last-child {
  margin-block-start: auto;
  align-self: flex-start;
  padding-block-start: 0.5rem;
}

.ndn-home-cta-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.75rem;
  align-items: center;
}

.ndn-home a.ndn-home-cta {
  text-decoration: none;
  border-radius: 999px;
  border: 1px solid var(--ndn-color-border-strong);
  color: var(--ndn-color-brand);
  padding-block: 0.8125rem;
  padding-inline: 1.625rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  transition: background-color var(--ndn-motion-duration-fast) ease,
    border-color var(--ndn-motion-duration-fast) ease,
    color var(--ndn-motion-duration-fast) ease;
}

.ndn-home a.ndn-home-cta:hover {
  background-color: var(--ndn-color-brand-wash);
  border-color: var(--ndn-color-brand);
  color: var(--ndn-color-brand-strong);
}

.ndn-home a.ndn-home-cta--primary {
  background-color: var(--ndn-color-brand);
  border-color: var(--ndn-color-brand);
  color: var(--ndn-color-surface-raised);
}

.ndn-home a.ndn-home-cta--primary:hover {
  background-color: var(--ndn-color-brand-strong);
  border-color: var(--ndn-color-brand-strong);
  color: var(--ndn-color-surface-raised);
}

.ndn-home-contact-number {
  font-family: var(--ndn-font-family-display);
  font-size: 1.75rem;
  font-weight: var(--ndn-font-weight-display);
  letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  margin-block: 0 1.5rem;
}
`;
---

{/* `wide`: this page's hero and alternating tinted bands are full-bleed and
    carry their own 68rem inner measure, so it opts out of the centred
    content column BaseLayout gives every other page. */}
<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  title={siteName}
  description={t('site.description', undefined, locale)}
  wide
>
  <div class="ndn-home">
    <section class="ndn-home-hero">
      <div class="ndn-home-inner">
        <div>
          <Heading level={1}>{t('home.hero.title', undefined, locale)}</Heading>
          <p class="ndn-home-lede">{t('home.hero.body', undefined, locale)}</p>
          <div class="ndn-home-cta-row">
            <Link
              href={whatsappChatUrl(whatsappBusinessNumber)}
              external
              className="ndn-home-cta ndn-home-cta--primary"
            >
              {t('home.hero.primaryCta', undefined, locale)}
            </Link>
            <Link href="#services" className="ndn-home-cta">
              {t('home.hero.secondaryCta', undefined, locale)}
            </Link>
          </div>
        </div>
        {/* Decorative, hence `alt=""`: the mark says nothing the headline
            beside it does not already say, and a description of it would be
            one more thing for a screen reader to read before the lede. */}
        <img
          class="ndn-home-hero-mark"
          src="/logo-mark.png"
          alt=""
          width="480"
          height="570"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="about" class="ndn-home-section" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <div class="ndn-home-inner ndn-home-prose">
        <Heading level={2} id="about-heading">{t('about.heading', undefined, locale)}</Heading>
        <p>{t('about.intro', undefined, locale)}</p>
        <p>{t('home.about.body', undefined, locale)}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="services"
      class="ndn-home-section ndn-home-section--tinted"
      aria-labelledby="services-heading"
    >
      <div class="ndn-home-inner">
        <Heading level={2} id="services-heading">
          {t('home.services.heading', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <p class="ndn-home-intro">{t('services.intro', undefined, locale)}</p>
        <div class="ndn-home-grid">
          {
            services.map((service) => (
              <Card>
                <Heading level={3}>{t(service.titleKey, undefined, locale)}</Heading>
                <p>{t(service.bodyKey, undefined, locale)}</p>
              </Card>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="blog" class="ndn-home-section" aria-labelledby="blog-heading">
      <div class="ndn-home-inner">
        <Heading level={2} id="blog-heading">{t('home.blog.heading', undefined, locale)}</Heading>
        <p class="ndn-home-intro">{t('home.blog.intro', undefined, locale)}</p>
        <div class="ndn-home-grid">
          {/* `client:load`, not `client:only` — the seed must be in the HTML
              for a crawler and for a reader with no JavaScript. Same
              reasoning, and the same directive, as the `/blog` listing. */}
          <LiveBlogList
            client:load
            locale={locale}
            initialPosts={postsForLocale}
            limit={HOME_LIST_LIMIT}
            headingLevel={3}
            strings={{
              empty: t('blog.index.empty', undefined, locale),
              readMore: t('blog.index.readMore', undefined, locale),
              // The placeholder survives into the island: `t()` runs here,
              // at build time, and cannot format a date for a post
              // published since. Same arrangement as `posterAltTemplate`.
              publishedOnTemplate: t('common.publishedOn', { date: '{date}' }, locale),
              readingTimeTemplate: t('blog.readingTime', { minutes: '{minutes}' }, locale),
            }}
          />
        </div>
        <div class="ndn-home-cta-row">
          <Link href={`/${locale}/blog`} className="ndn-home-cta">
            {t('home.blog.viewAll', undefined, locale)}
          </Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="workshops"
      class="ndn-home-section ndn-home-section--tinted"
      aria-labelledby="workshops-heading"
    >
      <div class="ndn-home-inner">
        <Heading level={2} id="workshops-heading">
          {t('home.workshops.heading', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <p class="ndn-home-intro">{t('home.workshops.intro', undefined, locale)}</p>
        <div class="ndn-home-grid">
          <LiveWorkshopList
            client:load
            locale={locale}
            initialWorkshops={workshopsForLocale}
            limit={HOME_LIST_LIMIT}
            headingLevel={3}
            strings={{
              empty: t('workshops.index.empty', undefined, locale),
              viewDetails: t('workshops.index.viewDetails', undefined, locale),
              posterAltTemplate: t('workshops.index.posterAlt', { title: '{title}' }, locale),
              publishedOnTemplate: t('common.announcedOn', { date: '{date}' }, locale),
              happeningLabel: t('workshops.index.happeningLabel', undefined, locale),
              zoneLabels: {
                india: t('workshops.time.india', undefined, locale),
                uk: t('workshops.time.uk', undefined, locale),
                middleEast: t('workshops.time.middleEast', undefined, locale),
              },
            }}
          />
        </div>
        <div class="ndn-home-cta-row">
          <Link href={`/${locale}/workshops`} className="ndn-home-cta">
            {t('home.workshops.viewAll', undefined, locale)}
          </Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="testimonials"
      class="ndn-home-section ndn-home-section--accent"
      aria-labelledby="testimonials-heading"
    >
      <div class="ndn-home-inner">
        <Heading level={2} id="testimonials-heading">
          {t('home.testimonials.heading', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <div class="ndn-home-grid">
          {/* 2026-09-07: `featuredOnly`, not `limit`. The owner: *"I want
              the principal clinician to have option to cherry pick top rated
              testimonials on the landing page."* Which quotes appear here,
              and how many, is now the principal's selection
              (`account/testimonials`) rather than "the newest three" — so
              this strip takes no count at all. Until anyone curates, the API
              ranks the newest three, which is exactly what this rendered
              before. */}
          <LiveTestimonialList
            client:load
            locale={locale}
            initialTestimonials={testimonials}
            featuredOnly
            strings={{
              empty: t('testimonials.index.empty', undefined, locale),
              anonymous: t('testimonials.form.attributionDisplay.anonymous', undefined, locale),
            }}
          />
        </div>
        <div class="ndn-home-cta-row">
          <Link href={`/${locale}/testimonials`} className="ndn-home-cta">
            {t('home.testimonials.viewAll', undefined, locale)}
          </Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="contact"
      class="ndn-home-section ndn-home-section--tinted"
      aria-labelledby="contact-heading"
    >
      <div class="ndn-home-inner">
        <Heading level={2} id="contact-heading">
          {t('common.getInTouch', undefined, locale)}
        </Heading>
        <p class="ndn-home-intro">{t('home.contact.body', undefined, locale)}</p>
        <p class="ndn-home-contact-number">{whatsappBusinessNumber}</p>
        <div class="ndn-home-cta-row">
          <Link
            href={whatsappChatUrl(whatsappBusinessNumber)}
            external
            className="ndn-home-cta ndn-home-cta--primary"
          >
            {t('home.hero.primaryCta', undefined, locale)}
          </Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <VisuallyHidden>{t('common.endOfPage', undefined, locale)}</VisuallyHidden>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style set:html={homeStylesCss} />
